{%- endif %}
{%- if database == 'sqlite' %} It keeps its data in SQLite (`src/db.ts`): on the platform the file is `/data/app.db` (`DATABASE_PATH`) on a volume that outlives the pod, backed up nightly; staging and production each have their own. Change the schema by adding `migrations/NNN_name.sql` (applied once each, in order, at startup); never edit one that has run. Image rollback does not reverse database migrations; review compatibility before promoting an older image.{% endif %}

## Callers and calling other apps

`src/platform.ts` holds what the platform gives the app ([calling another app](https://github.com/samclement/swhurl-platform/blob/main/docs/apps.md#calling-another-app)):
{% if kind == 'web' %}
- **Who is calling.** `identify(request.headers)` returns `{ type: "app", id: "<app>" }` for another app that sent a token the platform issued for this app alone, `{ type: "user", id: "<email>" }` for a signed-in person, or `anonymous`. A bad token throws `Unauthorized`, which `src/server.ts` answers with 401. Every log line and span carries `caller.type` and `caller.id`. For a route only apps may use, call `requireApp(caller)`.
{%- endif %}
- **Calling another app.** Add `calls: [orders]` to `swhurl.yaml` before the app is created (afterwards: `make app-calls` on the platform, or the app page's **Calls** form). Then `await service("orders").fetch("/path")` reaches the same environment's `orders` with this app's token for it; the callee's spans join the same trace.{% if kind == 'web' %} `GET /call/orders` in `src/server.ts` is an example to replace.{% endif %}

## Events

`src/events.ts` publishes and receives events on the platform's NATS ([events](https://github.com/samclement/swhurl-platform/blob/main/docs/apps.md#events)). Declare them in `swhurl.yaml` before the app is created (afterwards: `make app-events` on the platform):

```yaml
events:
  publish: [created]               # other apps see {{ app_name }}.created
  subscribe: [orders.created]      # <app>.<event>
```

Then `await publish("created", data)` and `await subscribe("orders.created", async (event) => { ... })`. An event is a CloudEvents envelope (`event.data` is what was published); a handler runs inside the publisher's trace, and if it throws the event comes back, five tries in all. {% if kind == 'web' %}`src/server.ts` publishes the first declared event on every request and logs every event it subscribes to{% else %}`src/worker.ts` logs every event it subscribes to{% endif %}: examples to replace. `subscribe` keeps trying until it is receiving, since a new app can start before NATS knows it. Locally there is no NATS: `publish` returns `null` and `subscribe` never calls back.

## Without the platform

Locally there are no platform keys or tokens: {% if kind == 'web' %}requests without a token work as before and a request with one is refused; {% endif %}to call another app, set `SWHURL_SERVICE_<NAME>_URL` to a local stub.

## Local development

```bash
npm install
npm run dev                             # the SDK stays off locally (the image turns it on)
{%- if kind == 'web' %}
curl http://localhost:8080/healthz
{%- endif %}
npm run check                           # type-check, as CI does
npm run build && npm test               # the tests run against the built app
```
{%- if database == 'sqlite' %}

Locally the database is `app.db` in this directory (ignored by Git); delete it to start again.
{%- endif %}

To see telemetry locally, `npm run build`, then `OTEL_TRACES_EXPORTER=console node --import ./dist/instrumentation.js dist/main.js` prints spans (or run an OpenTelemetry collector on `localhost:4318` and drop the variable).
